WEBVTT

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:07.480
My wounds aren't healing...

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:16.830
Fuyumi...

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:55.260
Beyond this point is the Southern Demon World.

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:57.560
It's connected to the Dimensional Highway.

00:01:58.090 --> 00:02:01.100
So we'll be taking a transport service back to the Eastern Demon District from there?

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:04.990
No, heroes can't just sit around all day.

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:07.480
We'll hit 'em by surprise.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:11.920
Our destination is the Demon World's Acropolis,

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:13.860
where my brother is.

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:19.860
Targets verified.

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:23.870
Well folks, this is the moment we've been waiting for!

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:30.370
It's time for us, Team Fearless, the true vampire hunters to shine!

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:35.380
From Neyn?

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:40.090
Staz and that girl escaped?!

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:47.090
Indeed, we are vampire hunters,

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:50.350
but we have yet to hunt down one vampire.

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:54.110
Then isn't our leader just a fraud?

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:57.360
Huh? What were we just talking about?

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:00.010
Bad!

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:02.720
Maybe we're the only vampire hunters around because

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:06.420
we're so strong that we don't have any opposition!

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:08.700
I bet we could totally take a vampire down.

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:12.830
Basically, it's a positive outlook on our group.

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:17.900
Well, if we really could take down a vampire, we'd 
become top class demons in the Demon World's Acropolis.

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:20.500
In that case, we have to do it even if everything's just a lie.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:21.840
However!

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:24.690
Our target this time is <i>that</i> vampire!

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:28.030
And he's the real deal without a doubt!

00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:29.180
Which means...

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:31.020
We have no hopes of winning?

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:31.850
Bad!

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:33.090
This is our chance!

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:36.500
If we actually manage to hunt down a vampire,

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:39.110
it'd be our best opportunity to become famous!

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:41.110
Let's get going, folks!

00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:45.490
We'll prove that our title as vampire hunters isn't just for show!

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:48.180
Sam, that's such a nice watch!

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:50.740
Ah, I see it's caught your eye.

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:52.880
It's quite rare, you know?

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:53.960
So sleepy...

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:56.140
Was it expensive?

00:03:56.140 --> 00:03:57.370
Kinda.

00:03:57.370 --> 00:04:01.330
But you always need to pay more for good stuff...{But the good stuff always fetches higher prices...}

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:03.680
For instance, something like this!

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:05.890
Hey, I'm gonna take a nap.

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:08.970
Wake me up if anything happens, leader.

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:12.230
I can't believe you guys!

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:14.940
That's the last straw! I'm going alone!{That tears it, I'm going alone!}

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:17.160
I'm gonna take care of everything myself!

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:18.720
I'll have you guys remember this!

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:24.190
<i>What was everyone doing?!</i>

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:25.820
<i>I'm supposed to be their leader!</i>

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:27.370
<i>And these nameplates...</i>

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:30.700
<i>I even stayed up the entire night to make one for everyone so they'd be remembered.</i>

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:32.970
<i>I've realized...</i>

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:39.340
<i>that they'll only listen to me when I activate my ability!</i>

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:43.550
<i>I didn't want to do this. In fact, I'd prefer if I </i>never<i> did this.</i>

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:47.220
<i>But this time, our target is a vampire.</i>

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.850
<i>I can't afford to relax here.</i>

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:52.660
<i>So I need to stay on my toes.</i>

00:04:54.350 --> 00:05:00.110
My, my. Having to put up this act every time we need our leader to do reconnaissance is a real pain.

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:01.820
There's no other choice.

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:08.430
Our leader has to do his part first or else we can't pitch in.

00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:12.610
It can't be helped since he says he doesn't want to do it if he has a choice.

00:05:12.610 --> 00:05:16.290
Regardless of what he says, he <i>is</i> our leader after all.

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:20.420
By the way, can we take off our nameplates now?

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:22.920
It suits you!

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:24.510
It totally suits you!

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:27.110
Especially those sunglasses!

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:31.420
Can we stop playing around?

00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:33.350
You need to get yourself a pistol!

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:35.280
{I think you're overreacting...}I think you are too rowdy.

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:39.480
Weren't we supposed to keep a low profile in other demons' territories?

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:44.170
You need to be wild to blend in with demons in the Demon World.

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:45.950
Here, try holding this.

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:49.990
You're enjoying this way too much.

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:52.990
There aren't any bullets in this gun, right?

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:54.620
{Shouldn't it be obvious?}Obviously.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.400
It's just a toy.

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:57.520
What's that you're holding?

00:05:58.630 --> 00:06:00.710
When I'm not keeping an eye on you,

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:02.840
this rope lets me know exactly where you are.

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:08.460
T-This feels like I'm about to be sold off somewhere.

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:12.600
Relax. I wouldn't sell you even if they offered me a fortune.

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:15.100
Here.

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:16.670
Thank you very much.

00:06:16.670 --> 00:06:18.850
Targets in sight.

00:06:19.070 --> 00:06:22.510
Yuck. They're eating canned beans.

00:06:22.510 --> 00:06:24.730
I can't stand guys like that.

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:29.490
What an awful guy to force a girl to eat that stuff.{Forcing a girl to eat that stuff... What an awful guy.}

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:32.020
What? You don't like beans?

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:35.240
N-No... that's not it.

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:38.120
If she says it like that, she hates 'em.

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:42.500
Um... It's a little embarrassing to ask for this...

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:49.980
Well... Staz-san... I'd really like to...

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:51.970
suck some of your blood. {:O}

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:53.140
No.

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:55.770
Just a little bit should be fine, right?

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:59.090
You still have a little left from earlier, right? 
Just eat your beans already.

00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:04.680
Wh-What happened? The atmosphere just got awkward...

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:06.400
How pitiful.

00:07:08.140 --> 00:07:10.370
Yo! Haven't seen you around.

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:11.480
Are you a wanderer?

00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:13.950
U-Um no... I'm just...

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:16.540
This is my sunny-side spot, you know?

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:19.430
Oh, sorry. I didn't know.

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:20.920
Nah, it's cool.

00:07:21.490 --> 00:07:23.000
Take a look at my stash.

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:24.170
I've got some good stuff.

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:26.050
I-Is that...

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:27.560
catnip?!

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:31.180
It's the bargaining chip we use around here.

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:32.520
You'll get hooked.

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:34.210
You're a bad cat!

00:07:34.210 --> 00:07:35.180
What are you talking about?

00:07:35.570 --> 00:07:37.430
I can tell, you know?

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:40.650
You've used some before too, haven't you?{Lol. It's like crack}

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:44.470
Well... Maybe...

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:46.480
Take a look.

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:48.360
That girl is in the same boat.

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:51.650
Once you get a taste of it, you'll never forget.

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:58.160
<i>So that's why that chick is being so 
obedient even while she's being abducted!</i>

00:08:00.630 --> 00:08:02.410
<i>He won't get away with this.</i>

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:04.820
<i>That guy is extremely ruthless.</i>

00:08:04.820 --> 00:08:09.380
<i>Looks like I'll have to activate my ability.</i>

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:13.170
I won't let you die peacefully!

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:16.210
You'll die a horrible death and—

00:08:16.210 --> 00:08:20.100
Huh? Why do I suddenly feel so good?

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:27.150
This is the result of your puny magic vessel's capabilities

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:31.210
after receiving some magic from me.

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:35.700
You're holding onto more magic than your vessel can withstand.

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:40.020
The amount of time you have between each dose of magic you need is gradually becoming shorter.

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:42.740
Eventually, you might not even be able to last for more than a minute.

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:46.830
That's why I'm against you sucking my blood unless it's an emergency.

00:08:47.390 --> 00:08:50.300
I pretty much understand now, but...

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:53.800
I think it's kind of an emergency now.{>_>}

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:56.820
You're starting to disappear! Why didn't you say so sooner?!

00:08:56.820 --> 00:08:58.260
That's what I was trying to—

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:00.960
You idiot! When you're desperate, you have to act like it!

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:04.020
You need to be screaming, "Help! I'm dying!"

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:05.020
You want to be resurrected, don't you?!

00:09:19.760 --> 00:09:22.370
I bet you just opened your mouth thinking I'd put it in, right?

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:25.070
I told you.

00:09:25.070 --> 00:09:26.960
I'm not resurrecting you because <i>I</i> want to.

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:31.540
I'm resurrecting you only because <i>you</i> desire it.

00:09:31.540 --> 00:09:36.470
Show your desires in a way a dunce like me can understand.

00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:38.970
You want some of my blood, right?

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:42.390
If so, my finger is right here.

00:09:57.190 --> 00:09:58.280
Hey...

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:01.330
That's enough already! I understand now.

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:02.780
I told you to stop!

00:10:02.780 --> 00:10:04.460
You're going overboard!

00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:06.780
Seriously, my finger's being drained!

00:10:07.090 --> 00:10:09.420
Are you even conscious?

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:16.930
<i>This isn't good...</i>

00:10:16.930 --> 00:10:19.310
<i>She's not going to be able to last for long.</i>

00:10:19.310 --> 00:10:21.110
<i>If I don't do something...{Something has to be done.}{Did I hear shine in this line?}</i>

00:10:24.110 --> 00:10:25.560
Listen up, folks!

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:31.810
Yesterday, I single-handedly attacked the target and almost took him down!

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:35.000
Huh? Why come back if I could've finished him off?

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:36.780
I can't blame you if you're thinking that.

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:37.430
Bad!

00:10:37.430 --> 00:10:39.700
I had remembered!

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:44.520
We are a team!

00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:49.000
When we undertake a task as a team, we must finish as a team!

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:52.840
More like you got high on catnip, fell asleep,{More like you got high off of catnip, fell asleep,}

00:10:52.840 --> 00:10:57.670
lost track of the target, got yourself lost and came back.

00:10:57.670 --> 00:11:00.020
Roy, did you say something?

00:11:00.020 --> 00:11:03.060
Huh, I must be sleep talking again.

00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:05.500
So anyway, leader,

00:11:05.500 --> 00:11:08.140
that part of the job should be finished, right?

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:10.570
U-Uh, well...

00:11:10.570 --> 00:11:11.880
Actually, not yet...

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:15.230
Did you just click your tongue?

00:11:15.230 --> 00:11:18.600
And what are you mumbling about? I can't understand you.

00:11:18.930 --> 00:11:23.240
Well, what's important is that you're on your way to finish it, right?

00:11:25.880 --> 00:11:27.240
Right?

00:11:27.740 --> 00:11:29.810
O-Of course...

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:35.170
Let's see...

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:38.480
Should we go buy some magic drinks before we head off?

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:40.190
It might not be strong enough though.

00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:42.330
R-Right.{O-Oh, that's right.}

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:47.030
You haven't looked me in the eye since you woke up.

00:11:47.030 --> 00:11:48.480
What is it this time?

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:50.710
Well... Um...

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:55.850
I feel awkward and embarrassed when I think about what happened yesterday.

00:11:55.850 --> 00:11:56.650
Huh?

00:11:57.260 --> 00:12:00.150
It's nothing. Don't mind me.

00:12:00.470 --> 00:12:02.500
What are you talking about?

00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:07.210
If it's what you wanted, why would it embarrass you?

00:12:07.210 --> 00:12:09.370
It's a process that'll help you get resurrected.

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:11.430
I know, but...

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:15.500
I was kind of surprised at myself for being so bold.

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:19.490
Well, you <i>were</i> surprisingly aggressive.

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:23.170
Let's talk about something else already!

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:26.970
S-So cute!

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:29.600
It's a little kitty, Staz-san!

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:31.350
I'm gonna go pet it.

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:37.290
You'd better not. It's a cat from the Demon World.

00:12:37.290 --> 00:12:39.610
What'll happen if you go too close carelessly and get eaten?

00:12:39.910 --> 00:12:41.490
Oh, you're just exaggerating.

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:42.650
<i>Bad!{lol I love him}</i>

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:44.410
<i>This guy is good.</i>

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:47.990
<i>I can't let him get the best of me!</i>

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:52.060
<i>I'll toss my pride aside for the sake of my team!</i>

00:12:52.060 --> 00:12:54.000
<i>I'm going all out!</i>

00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:55.750
Look, look!

00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:57.740
It's so friendly!

00:12:57.740 --> 00:12:59.630
It likes you, Staz-san!

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:01.850
Jeez. Why is it being so annoying?

00:13:01.850 --> 00:13:03.920
What's with this thing?!

00:13:03.920 --> 00:13:05.930
That tickles!

00:13:08.980 --> 00:13:10.430
That hurt, bastard!

00:13:14.690 --> 00:13:15.940
Tastes good.

00:13:17.120 --> 00:13:18.420
The cat just...

00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:20.070
It turned into a person.

00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:25.210
Fools! You got tricked so easily!

00:13:25.210 --> 00:13:26.950
I am not a cat!

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:29.940
Nah, you were totally a cat just now.

00:13:29.940 --> 00:13:31.540
That was definitely a cat.

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:34.080
That wasn't my real form!

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:36.990
He was purring exactly like one.

00:13:36.990 --> 00:13:38.580
He even meowed like one.

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:41.630
Oh, shut up already! I'm—

00:13:43.820 --> 00:13:46.100
Hair got stuck in my mouth...

00:13:46.610 --> 00:13:47.990
I feel sick.{Nasty...}

00:13:47.990 --> 00:13:49.510
Then why'd you eat it?

00:13:49.980 --> 00:13:52.390
I don't know what you're up to, but you're irritating me.

00:13:52.750 --> 00:13:55.030
Explain what you were trying to do!{Explain what's the meaning of this is.}

00:13:55.390 --> 00:13:56.640
Are you an enemy?

00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:59.610
If that's the case, I won't show you any mercy.

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:00.740
<i>Bad!</i>

00:14:00.740 --> 00:14:03.060
<i>This guy is short-tempered.</i>

00:14:03.060 --> 00:14:05.860
<i>What in the world is taking my team so long?!</i>

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:09.870
<i>If they keep dawdling, I'll just have to...</i>

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:14.260
<i>Finish him off myself.</i>

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:16.870
Staz-san, why did you suddenly attack him?

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:19.250
<i>This guy managed to dodge it.</i>

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:24.760
<i>It seemed like he knew what sort of attack I would use and which direction it was coming from when he evaded it.{The way he evaded it even seemed like he knew exactly which direction I was attacking from.}</i>

00:14:25.080 --> 00:14:26.080
Bad!

00:14:26.500 --> 00:14:29.510
Calling me an enemy isn't exactly the right term.

00:14:29.510 --> 00:14:33.640
Let it be known that this is a one-sided hunt.

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:36.640
A vampire hunt.

00:14:40.780 --> 00:14:44.060
We are Team Fearless.

00:14:48.540 --> 00:14:52.150
You understand?

00:14:57.370 --> 00:15:00.870
What took you guys so long?!

00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:02.760
My apologies.

00:15:02.760 --> 00:15:05.230
Sam was taking a long time in the bathroom.

00:15:05.230 --> 00:15:06.840
Why didn't you pick up the pace?!

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:08.520
<i>What's with these guys?</i>

00:15:08.520 --> 00:15:10.590
<i>Did they come here to pick a fight with me?</i>

00:15:11.490 --> 00:15:13.870
Was the hair yummy?

00:15:13.870 --> 00:15:16.370
I'm not eating it because I want to!

00:15:16.370 --> 00:15:17.220
Take it easy.

00:15:17.510 --> 00:15:19.460
<i>They said they were a team and yet,</i>

00:15:19.460 --> 00:15:21.980
<i>they're ignoring us and arguing amongst themselves.</i>

00:15:22.370 --> 00:15:24.360
<i>We should make a break for it before this gets even more troublesome.</i>

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:31.200
See? We were bickering so much our target wanted to escape.

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:32.410
Huh? How did you know?

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:33.740
I haven't even...

00:15:34.050 --> 00:15:36.160
I can tell.

00:15:36.610 --> 00:15:39.270
My ability is called Reader.

00:15:39.270 --> 00:15:41.840
As long as I have a piece of my victim within me,

00:15:41.840 --> 00:15:45.000
I'm able to read all of your movements.

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:47.610
And my ability is...

00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:49.070
That should do.

00:15:49.070 --> 00:15:50.610
Good night.

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:54.850
Roy's ability is Chat Room.

00:15:55.510 --> 00:16:00.390
It allows me to share my reading info amongst the team.

00:16:06.430 --> 00:16:07.380
Oh, right.

00:16:07.380 --> 00:16:09.900
So what that means is...

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:11.320
That sure looks fun.

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:13.410
It sure is.

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:16.040
And what about the rest of your team's abilities?

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:21.050
An ability capable of killing me?

00:16:24.340 --> 00:16:26.170
Precisely.

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:31.970
Interesting.

00:16:32.870 --> 00:16:34.970
I'd like to see you try.

00:16:37.130 --> 00:16:38.560
What's this?

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:44.050
Come on. Don't tell me you thought such a weak blow was going to kill me.

00:16:44.050 --> 00:16:45.560
Don't look down on me.

00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:48.520
Say something already, you wimps!

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:53.780
You can read my movements, right?

00:16:53.780 --> 00:16:56.200
Then try to dodge all of my attacks!

00:16:56.200 --> 00:17:01.920
It's not like... your attacks can affect me!

00:17:21.830 --> 00:17:23.680
Come on! What's wrong?!

00:17:23.680 --> 00:17:27.060
Your attacks aren't reaching me at all!

00:17:27.340 --> 00:17:30.480
You guys need to turn it up a notch!

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:33.440
Use a jet stream attack or something!

00:17:33.440 --> 00:17:36.820
No, that won't be necessary.

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:40.000
Huh? What happened to your enthusiasm?

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:42.540
You guys didn't even put up a fight.

00:17:42.810 --> 00:17:44.000
I can't believe it.

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:45.540
He still hasn't noticed.

00:17:46.370 --> 00:17:49.780
I've always wanted a hat like this.

00:17:49.780 --> 00:17:51.800
Isn't this a ten gallon hat?

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:57.370
Well then, we'll be taking our leave.

00:17:57.800 --> 00:17:59.470
Hey!

00:17:59.780 --> 00:18:00.470
Fuyumi!

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:01.470
Where are you?!

00:18:01.940 --> 00:18:03.050
Answer me!

00:18:03.050 --> 00:18:04.360
Fuyumi!

00:18:06.280 --> 00:18:07.480
This is...

00:18:09.010 --> 00:18:10.340
You're kidding me.

00:18:10.340 --> 00:18:12.230
My wounds aren't healing.

00:18:17.650 --> 00:18:21.840
Now, just leave it to Roy's and my abilities to finish things off.

00:18:40.580 --> 00:18:42.290
Dammit...

00:18:42.290 --> 00:18:43.760
It hurts...

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:45.350
Where are you...

00:18:46.400 --> 00:18:47.640
Fuyumi?

00:18:55.020 --> 00:18:56.530
Relax.

00:18:56.870 --> 00:19:02.130
If you behave yourself in there, I'll return you unharmed.

00:19:02.130 --> 00:19:05.540
After we eliminate the vampire, that is.

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:08.960
You don't need to take me back. Just let me out from here!

00:19:09.490 --> 00:19:13.020
Your voice can't reach him even if you scream.

00:19:15.020 --> 00:19:18.140
It seems like he's still searching for the girl.

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:24.210
<i>This is what I get for relying on that rope.</i>

00:19:24.980 --> 00:19:27.050
<i>Absolutely nothing has changed.</i>

00:19:27.050 --> 00:19:29.400
<i>What kinda dark hero am I?!{What was that dark hero nonsense?!}</i>

00:19:36.830 --> 00:19:38.440
Bastard!

00:19:40.440 --> 00:19:42.570
Sweet. It hit.

00:19:42.570 --> 00:19:43.940
See ya.

00:19:47.090 --> 00:19:48.280
<i>No way...</i>

00:19:48.280 --> 00:19:50.090
<i>I've lost way too much blood.</i>

00:19:50.090 --> 00:19:52.490
<i>At this rate, I might end up dying.</i>

00:19:53.380 --> 00:19:55.180
<i>It's too soon...</i>

00:19:55.180 --> 00:19:58.560
<i>Was I always this weak?</i>

00:19:59.210 --> 00:20:00.380
<i>Seriously?</i>

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:02.840
<i>Why was I going on about all that dark hero crap?</i>

00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:04.890
This was unexpected.

00:20:04.890 --> 00:20:06.370
He was pretty weak.

00:20:06.370 --> 00:20:07.850
Shall we finish him off?

00:20:07.850 --> 00:20:09.350
Let's do it.

00:20:09.630 --> 00:20:12.270
Seems like vampires weren't that big of a deal after all.

00:20:12.270 --> 00:20:17.860
What are you talking about? It's just that no one can stand up to our teamwork.

00:20:38.380 --> 00:20:39.710
Fuyumi...

00:20:40.040 --> 00:20:41.890
What was that just now?!

00:20:41.890 --> 00:20:44.970
Rand's head just sounded off like a firecracker!{lol}

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:47.930
Rand! Hey! Rand, what's wrong? Rand!

00:20:47.930 --> 00:20:48.980
Say something!

00:20:48.980 --> 00:20:50.720
What happened to you?

00:20:59.230 --> 00:21:00.170
Impossible!

00:21:00.170 --> 00:21:02.160
He was almost out cold a second ago!

00:21:03.140 --> 00:21:05.240
Where's he getting all that strength from?!

00:21:14.870 --> 00:21:16.170
I've figured it out.

00:21:19.910 --> 00:21:22.170
What have you figured out?

00:21:22.170 --> 00:21:24.840
Perhaps it was your own death.

00:21:25.560 --> 00:21:27.090
Exactly.

00:21:27.410 --> 00:21:29.350
At this rate, I'll end up dying.

00:21:29.350 --> 00:21:32.860
That's why I sealed my wounds with magic.

00:21:32.860 --> 00:21:35.600
I-It's stuck!

00:21:35.600 --> 00:21:37.630
And it occurred to me...

00:21:37.630 --> 00:21:40.860
In order to restore my strength,

00:21:43.940 --> 00:21:46.260
I can just feast on your magic.

00:21:47.330 --> 00:21:48.360
No...

00:21:48.360 --> 00:21:51.370
My strength is being sapped...

00:21:54.830 --> 00:21:59.670
This hand of mine isn't supposed to be used to crush my enemies.

00:21:59.670 --> 00:22:03.340
It's supposed to be used to protect things valuable to me.

00:22:05.910 --> 00:22:08.840
You understand?

00:22:10.580 --> 00:22:13.720
Where did you hide my precious possession?

00:22:19.380 --> 00:22:20.720
Right over there.

00:22:21.080 --> 00:22:22.270
Where?!

00:22:22.270 --> 00:22:24.110
Right inside of that...

00:22:27.110 --> 00:22:29.120
I was just kidding! She's not there!

00:22:29.120 --> 00:22:29.990
Huh?

00:22:29.990 --> 00:22:32.490
T-That wasn't it. What I meant to say was...{He's the best!}

00:22:32.490 --> 00:22:33.290
Huh?!

00:22:33.670 --> 00:22:35.070
I'm sorry...

00:22:39.050 --> 00:22:40.100
Staz-san!

00:22:40.100 --> 00:22:42.300
Whoa, don't point it at me.

00:22:42.300 --> 00:22:43.860
You're okay!

00:22:43.860 --> 00:22:47.590
And this gun had bullets in it after all!

00:22:47.590 --> 00:22:49.480
Besides that...

00:22:49.480 --> 00:22:50.910
Are you all right?

00:22:51.570 --> 00:22:53.350
Don't call me leader right now...

00:23:34.650 --> 00:23:37.390
You guys actually have a decent vehicle.

00:23:37.390 --> 00:23:39.390
So it may seem.

00:23:39.390 --> 00:23:41.720
You just came in uninvited,{Not just you had come uninvited,}

00:23:41.720 --> 00:23:44.590
made yourself at home, and now you're eating our fruits.

00:23:44.590 --> 00:23:45.930
What's up with you?

00:23:45.930 --> 00:23:47.690
Wanna complain or something?

00:23:47.690 --> 00:23:53.030
Aren't these the thank-you-for-not-killing-us fruits?

00:23:53.900 --> 00:23:55.780
<i>This guy's getting carried away!</i>

00:23:56.250 --> 00:23:57.680
Hey, Staz-san!

00:23:57.680 --> 00:23:59.540
Well then, please enjoy your stay.

00:24:01.490 --> 00:24:03.330
How are those two doing?

00:24:03.810 --> 00:24:06.570
For the time being, they are fine.

00:24:06.570 --> 00:24:11.440
but the vampire has fully recovered due to all the magic he sucked from them.

00:24:11.440 --> 00:24:14.540
It seems they will take some time to recover.

00:24:15.180 --> 00:24:19.020
But if our targets are onboard our ship,

00:24:19.020 --> 00:24:21.650
that means we still have a chance.

00:24:21.650 --> 00:24:23.190
Let's buy some time.

00:24:24.630 --> 00:24:26.400
A chance?

00:24:26.400 --> 00:24:27.470
Yeah.

00:24:28.440 --> 00:24:32.460
Usually, getting into the Demon World's Acropolis is difficult.

00:24:32.960 --> 00:24:35.520
Even if I still manage to get in somehow,

00:24:35.520 --> 00:24:37.950
I can't say the same for you.

00:24:37.950 --> 00:24:39.680
Huh? Then...

00:24:39.680 --> 00:24:41.610
Trespassing...

00:24:39.680 --> 00:24:41.610
Trespassing?

00:24:41.610 --> 00:24:43.220
is how we'll be getting in.

00:24:43.220 --> 00:24:45.710
And this airship is perfect for it.

00:24:46.120 --> 00:24:48.100
What was it called again?

00:24:48.880 --> 00:24:51.650
A wife sawer?{A life saver?}{What did she say?}

00:26:27.260 --> 00:26:29.340
This is Point N, N-1.

00:26:29.340 --> 00:26:31.230
Our radar has detected a signal.

00:26:31.650 --> 00:26:34.230
I believe we have intruders.

00:26:34.750 --> 00:26:36.740
Uninvited guests, huh?

00:26:36.740 --> 00:26:39.490
Okay, okay! Welcome!

00:26:39.830 --> 00:26:44.490
My right hand crab is ready to greet anyone at any time!

00:26:48.510 --> 00:26:50.670
Don't worry, Fuyumi.

00:26:50.670 --> 00:26:52.980
I won't ever let you go again.

00:26:52.980 --> 00:26:54.710
Wait, Staz-san!

00:26:55.330 --> 00:26:58.640
Are you sure it's fine to let them go?

00:26:58.640 --> 00:27:00.890
It's not like they can jump that far.

00:27:01.260 --> 00:27:05.890
I stuck a tracer on them, so we can find them once they fall.

00:27:05.890 --> 00:27:08.350
Now then, here we go!

00:27:09.310 --> 00:27:10.310
He's here!

00:27:10.310 --> 00:27:12.560
He's here! He's here! He's here!

00:27:12.560 --> 00:27:14.070
Welcome!

00:27:14.070 --> 00:27:16.940
Welcome to the Demon World's Acropolis!

00:27:26.210 --> 00:27:28.500
Thanks for the pick up!

00:27:28.760 --> 00:27:31.940
Roy, this isn't what you said would happen.

00:27:32.430 --> 00:27:35.750
He's going to reach the Demon World's Acropolis at this rate.

00:27:36.030 --> 00:27:38.000
The plan was foolproof...

00:27:38.000 --> 00:27:39.260
But the guard...

00:27:39.890 --> 00:27:43.510
was a bigger fool than I expected.
